# Operator reference data (SSH, Droplet, repo paths)

## Always consult

When instructions involve **SSH**, **`scp`**, **Droplet**, **repo paths on the server**, or **`REMOTE_PATH` / `DROPLET_REMOTE_PATH`**:

1. Read **`docs/OPERATOR-PRIVATE-NOTES.example.md`** (committed template — field list + command patterns).
2. If **`docs/OPERATOR-PRIVATE-NOTES.md`** exists in the workspace, read it and **use those values** in copy-paste commands (IP, key path, `root` vs `deploy`, which of `/opt/parking-acquisition-agents` vs `/opt/workspaces/parkinglot`).

Do **not** invent placeholder hostnames like `your_droplet_ip` or paths like `/path/to/your_private_key.pem` when the gitignored file already has the real values.

## Keep the template current

When the conversation or repo work reveals **new stable non-secret facts** (e.g. a second clone path, script default, or a field we should track):

- **Add** a row or section to **`docs/OPERATOR-PRIVATE-NOTES.example.md`** (empty or example-only — never real secrets).
- Tell the user to **merge the same fact** into their **`docs/OPERATOR-PRIVATE-NOTES.md`** (gitignored) if they use it.

Secrets (**tokens, passwords, full `DATABASE_URL` with password**) stay in **`deploy/secrets.env`** only — not in these notes.

